.TH ZERODDS-SPY 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-spy \- subscribe to a DDS topic and dump samples
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-spy
[\fBsubscribe\fR]
\fB\-t\fR \fITOPIC\fR
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
[\fB\-x\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-type\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-decode\fR \fB\-\-type\-file\fR \fIIDL\fR [\fB\-\-dialect\fR \fINAME\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-spy
starts a DCPS runtime, subscribes to the given
.B \-\-topic
as untyped raw bytes, and prints metadata plus an optional hex snippet
for every incoming sample.
.PP
The
.B subscribe
sub-command is implicit when the first argument is a flag — the two
forms below are equivalent:
.PP
.RS
zerodds-spy subscribe -t Foo
.br
zerodds-spy -t Foo
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Topic name to subscribe (REQUIRED).
.TP
.BR \-\-type " " \fINAME\fR
Announce this IDL type directly. Default: discover and follow.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
Stop after N samples. Default: unlimited.
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Stop after duration: \fI5\fR, \fI30s\fR, \fI2m\fR, \fI1h\fR.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-hex " " \fIBYTES\fR
First BYTES of the payload as hex (0 disables). Default: 32.
.TP
.BR \-\-decode
Decode samples to typed JSON. Needs
.BR \-\-type\-file .
.TP
.BR \-\-type\-file " " \fIIDL\fR
Out-of-band IDL providing the types to decode.
.TP
.BR \-\-dialect " " \fINAME\fR
The wire dialect to decode in: \fIcyclone\fR, \fIrti\fR, \fIfastdds\fR,
\fIopendds\fR and the others \fBzerodds\-idlc generate \-\-dialect\fR takes.
Default: the configuration's \fBwire.codec_dialect\fR, itself \fIspecification\fR
unless set. The decoder does not infer it from the bytes;
a sample written in another dialect is reported, not accepted.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
The base configuration file; its sibling
.IR PATH .d/
holds drop-ins. Default: the system configuration directory
.RI ( /etc/zerodds
on Linux,
.I /usr/local/etc/zerodds
on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-record (1),
.BR zerodds-snitch (1),
.BR zerodds-pcap (1)
